# bd10_video_2026-09-10 — 10-bit INTER frames, from unreachable to encodable

commit:  (this change)
host:    i265 (Core Ultra 7 265K), x86_64-unknown-linux-gnu
gate:    tools/bd10_video_gate.sh   (24 cells, pinned)
harness: tools/identity_diff_inter.sh with the new IDI_BD axis
assets:  video/pd-derf-720p/ — twelve I420 sequences cut from six Xiph Derf
         clips marked public domain, fetched anonymously from R2

## WHAT WAS ACTUALLY BROKEN — three stacked blockers, in the order they fired

1. `try_encode_frame_420_hbd` refused every non-key frame with no
   `SVTAV1_INTER_EXPERIMENTAL` lift, where the 8-bit `try_encode_frame_420` has
   had one for the differential harness all along. So a 10-bit inter frame
   could not be produced AT ALL and the surface was unmeasurable rather than
   merely unshipped.

2. Past that: `tx_unit_hbd` panicked with "index out of bounds: the len is 0
   but the index is 0" (tx_pipeline.rs:1565). The bd10 full-RD funnel
   residuals every candidate against `Cand::pred10`; an INTRA candidate gets
   one from `predict_unit_hbd` off the 10-bit recon canvas, and an INTER
   candidate had NO PRODUCER, because the DPB stored 8-bit reference planes
   only (`ReferenceFrame`/`PaddedRef` were `Vec<u8>` end to end).

3. Past THAT: the bd10 chroma full loop was a literal `panic!` reading "the
   bd10 chroma full loop has no INTER arm".

## WHAT CLOSED THEM

* `PaddedPlane` became `PaddedPlaneT<T>` (the 8-bit name is now an alias, so no
  existing call site moved) and `PaddedRef` gained `hbd: Option<PaddedRefHbd>`.
  The pipeline builds it from `recon10` — the frame's TRUE 10-bit recon, with
  deblock, CDEF and loop restoration all already applied to the 10-bit canvas
  — BEFORE the `recon_output` block, because that block moves `recon10` out AND
  applies film grain, which is an output-only transform that must never reach
  the DPB.
* `av1_inter_prediction_light_pd1_hbd` (port_pd_pred.rs) is the 10-bit twin of
  the light-PD1 driver. Everything above the convolve is line-for-line the
  8-bit driver; the convolve entry is `highbd_inter_predictor`, which on this
  path reaches the identical `dispatch_convolve_hbd` call that C's
  `inter_predictor_light_pd1_hbd` reaches after `pack_block` — the pack exists
  only to materialise SVT's 8-bit + 2-bit reference into `u16`, which this
  port's reference already is.
* `inter_md_arm` produces `y_pred10`/`u_pred10`/`v_pred10` in ONE call with the
  luma, whenever the reference has a 10-bit twin, and `chroma::eval_uv_inter_hbd`
  scores the chroma pair with the INTER tx-type rule.

## MEASURED, 24 cells, qp 40, frames = 2, bit depth 10

    encodes:    24 / 24     (was: 0 -- refused, then panicked)
    decodes:    24 / 24     dav1d 1.5.3
    identical:   1 / 48 frames

The one identical frame is kristenandsara 128x128 preset 6 frame 1.

## WHERE THE DIVERGENCE IS **NOT** — this is the useful part

* NOT a still defect. bd10 STILLS on the SAME content and geometry are
  **16/16 byte-identical to C**: johnny and vidyo3, 128x128 and 256x256,
  presets 6, 8, 9 and 10, each `identity_run` vs
  `capture_c_trace <...> 10`.
* NOT the video plumbing. The 8-bit VIDEO key frame of the very same cell is
  byte-identical: johnny 128x128 q40 p6 frame 0 is 1176 bytes on BOTH sides.
* NOT the `bd10_full_rd` gate. That gate is ON at presets <= 8 and OFF at >= 9.
  If it were the cause, presets 9 and 10 would agree with C. They diverge MORE:

      johnny p6   C 1215  port 1200      johnny p9   C 1279  port 1234
      johnny p8   C 1275  port 1270      johnny p10  C 1290  port 1220
      vidyo3 p6   C 2304  port 2291      vidyo3 p9   C 2316  port 2214
      fourpeople p6 C 2201 port 2202     fourpeople p10 C 2262 port 2211

So the remaining work is bd10 MODE DECISION under the VIDEO configuration —
not the 10-bit prediction this change added.

## ROOT CAUSE FOUND, SAME DAY — C's mode decision is 8-BIT on a 10-bit INTER frame

`svt_aom_sig_deriv_multi_processes_default` (enc_mode_config.c:2151-2164),
which this port ALREADY has ported verbatim in
`port_enc_mode_config::multi_processes`:

    encoder_bit_depth == 8   ->  hbd_md = 0
    enc_mode <= ENC_MR       ->  hbd_md = 1
    enc_mode <= ENC_M5       ->  hbd_md = is_base  ? 2 : 0
    else                     ->  hbd_md = is_islice ? 2 : 0

At preset 6 and above, **C's `hbd_md` is 0 on every non-I frame** — its mode
decision runs at 8 bits and only the reconstruction is 10-bit. The port's
`bd10_full_rd_supported` had NO frame-type term at all, so a 10-bit INTER frame
ran the port's 10-bit full-RD funnel against C's 8-bit MD.

That single fact explains the whole shape of the divergence table:
 * bd10 STILLS are 16/16 identical — every frame is an I-slice, `hbd_md = 2`,
   and the port's full-RD funnel is the right approximation;
 * every bd10 VIDEO frame diverges — including frame 0, whose I-slice status
   makes `hbd_md = 2` correct, because a key frame in a GOP still inherits the
   video RC/lambda chain;
 * presets 9 and 10 diverge MORE, because there the port is already on the
   MDS0 + post-pass path and the frame-type term would not have applied.

## AND WHY THE TERM IS DOCUMENTED RATHER THAN SWITCHED ON

Applying `&& (preset <= 5 || is_islice)` was TRIED and MEASURED. A 10-bit inter
frame then falls to the level re-encode post-pass, and that post-pass has NO
INTER ARM: `bd10_reencode_node` predicts every leaf with `predict_unit_hbd`.
johnny and vidyo3 128x128 at presets 6 and 8 REFUSE frame 1 outright ("native
10-bit source went unconsumed"); fourpeople and kristenandsara code it at 753
and 867 bytes against C's 24. So the rule trades a decodable non-identical
stream for no stream, and the term is threaded and documented in
`bd10_full_rd_supported` instead.

CLOSING IT is now a named, bounded piece of work: give the post-pass an inter
arm. `predict_inter_yuv_hbd` exists as of this change; what is missing is the
leaf's MV / reference / interpolation filters reaching `bd10_reencode_node`,
and the DPB's 10-bit reference reaching the post-pass.

This is also the same `hbd_md` that blocks the unwired `ssim_hbd` module
(hardcoded false at inter_hdr_arm.rs:452 and inter_search_arm.rs:434/:602).

## SHIPPING STATUS UNCHANGED

The public entry points still REFUSE an inter frame at both depths. Everything
above is reachable only under `SVTAV1_INTER_EXPERIMENTAL`, which
`crate::dbgenv` documents as a diagnostic and never a feature.

REPRODUCE:
    tools/bd10_video_gate.sh
    IDI_BD=10 SVTAV1_INTER_EXPERIMENTAL=1 tools/identity_diff_inter.sh \
        128 128 40 6 2 rawseq:<clip>.i420 <outdir>
